# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-1 and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch that holds them. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the classes, the minutes, the read rules and the NO-GO rules. Push ONE tag at a time and wait for its run to finish (the workflow keeps one pending run; queued tags are cancelled). Never cancel a running card job.
# PL1 (SOFT): the SOLO prefill ladder and its busy twin on the production profile, image tp4-next2-1. prefill_ladder_solo: four real-code prompts of about 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens (as the server counts
# them), ONE request at a time with nothing else running, so there is no decoder for the Lever N governor to pace (the solo step is 16,384 tokens): the time to first token and the prefill rate of each rung, a 16-token
# answer. prefill_ladder_busy: the same four sizes (distinct prompts, so no rung finds its blocks cached), each arriving beside SEVEN decoders (4k prompts, ignore_eos), today's policy: TTFT, prefill tok/s, busy over solo,
# and the decoders' worst gap and progress inside the arrival's prefill window. Recorded, never gated. READ: `python3 scripts/ci/prefill_ladder_report.py <smoke results>` (the solo table beside the busy one with the ratio).
# TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (nothing else on the host); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. Duration (estimate): boot 10 minutes, solo 4 (about 98 s for the 254k rung), busy 14
# (about 180 s for its 254k rung at the governed share; the decoders' budgets 600 / 1500 / 4000 / 6000 tokens outlast each rung), 30 minutes in all; the box is 50.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo,prefill_ladder_busy
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=prefill ladder measurement: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=50
